course: dictionary
lesson: 12867
title: Enmity: being enemies
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Enmity is a formal word for a feeling of hate or strong dislike between people or groups. It means being enemies. The word enemy is a clue: enmity is the feeling that comes with being enemies.
explain: «There was enmity between the two families for many years.» The clues are for many years and between the two families. This is not a quick argument. It is a long, lasting bad feeling between two groups.
explain: «Forgiveness can end enmity.» If forgiving can end it, enmity must be a bad feeling that can stop. Test your meaning: swap in hate or strong dislike, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Enmity is a noun. Its plural is enmities.
fact: «Enmity» means a feeling of hate or strong dislike between people or groups, or the state of being enemies.
fact: «Bitter enmity» means very strong, painful hate that may last a long time.
fact: Enmity is a formal word. You will meet it in history books, old stories and the Bible.
fact: Jesus taught people to «love your enemies», an idea about how kindness and forgiveness can end enmity.
exercise: «There was enmity between the two families.» What does enmity mean? | A long journey | A happy meeting | A kind gift | *A feeling of hate between people
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to enmity? | *Hostility | Harvest | Friendship | Laughter
exercise: «Forgiveness can end enmity.» What does this sentence suggest? | *Saying sorry and forgiving can stop people being enemies | Enemies always become friends by chance | Forgiveness is never useful | Forgiveness makes enmity grow stronger
test: What is the plural of enmity? | enmitys | enmityes | *enmities
test: «Their bitter enmity lasted for generations.» What does bitter suggest? | *Very strong and painful dislike | Sweet and kind | Sour, like a lemon | Fresh and new
exam: «The two rival teams had shown enmity for years, until they shook hands.» What does enmity mean? | A friendly game | *A feeling of hate between rivals | A new school rule | A shared dinner
